{# Right after the filters panel of the search (templates/case/search.html.twig), which the server always sends open: below
   lg, when the server marked it data-jus-filters-active="false" (no filter applied, no field with an error), this folds it
   as soon as it is parsed, before the first paint, so the results come first and nothing moves once the page shows.
   Without JavaScript the panel stays open. The query is Bootstrap's lg breakpoint, as in assets/behaviours/filters-panel.ts,
   which opens a folded panel again when the window grows to lg. A script policy (CSP) would need a hash or a nonce for
   this script, as for the theme script in the head (templates/_theme_script.html.twig). The tests run this very file
   (assets/behaviours/filters-inline-script.test.ts): keep the one <script> and no Twig inside it. #}
<script>(() => { if (!matchMedia('(max-width: 991.98px)').matches) return; for (const panel of document.querySelectorAll('details.jus-filters[data-jus-filters-active="false"]')) panel.open = false; })();</script>
